<title>UK: Saudi produced 8.01 million bpd in November - OPEC.</title>
<headline>Saudi produced 8.01 million bpd in November - OPEC.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabia told OPEC it produced 8.01 million barrels per day (bpd) in November, not far from its 8.0 million bod OPEC quota, the OPEC News Agency (OPECNA) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>But the kingdom, OPEC and the world's largest oil producer, said its supply to the market was right on quota.</p>
<p>OPEC sets its individual quotas according to supply to the market rather than wellhead production.</p>
<p>Supply, as defined by OPEC, is calculated as domestic consumption, plus net export sales of crude and products, plus withdrawals of stocks held outside national boundaries.</p>
<p>Production and supply data for the month of November received so far by the OPEC Secretariat from member countries is as follows (in thousand bpd):  </p>
<p>  Country	Production	Supply</p>
<p>  Algeria	  795.0	   773.0</p>
<p>  Indonesia    1,327.4	    N/A</p>
<p>  Iran	   3,597.0	 3,597.0</p>
<p>  Iraq	     725.0	   725.0</p>
<p>  Kuwait	 2,009.5	 2,010.3</p>
<p>  Libya	  1,400.0	 1,400.0</p>
<p>  Nigeria	1,865.0	 1,865.0</p>
<p>  Qatar	    392.2	   382.3</p>
<p>  Saudi Arabia 8,012.3	 8,001.6</p>
<p>N/A - not available</p>
<p>--London newsroom, +44 171 542 6280</p>
</text>
